window.ENCYCLOPEDIA_ENTRY_BODIES["chapter-map-sector-scene-bundles"] = "## Chapter Status\n- Maturity: `draft-narrative`\n- Scope: `ROM knowledge`\n- Scope meaning: Facts about EarthBound's original data, routines, runtime behavior, or asset contracts.\n- Source root: `bundled-private-reference`\n- Primary evidence notes: 6\n- Additional related notes: 10\n## Sector Root\nThe map scene layer starts with the fixed `40x32` world-sector grid: `1280` sectors. Each sector can now be addressed as a stable scene row rather than inferred from a raw map coordinate window.\nThe sector bundle contract joins sector metadata, placed objects, tileset dependencies, door and trigger records, enemy-map groups, music options, hotspots, map-change group counts, and per-sector `map_tiles.map` hashes.\n## Current Inventory\n- `1280` sector rows exist.\n- `627` sectors contain placed objects.\n- `1582` placed object IDs are joined into sector rows.\n- `2080` trigger records span `601` sectors.\n- `1072` doors span `519` sectors.\n- `220` object triggers span `100` sectors.\n- `56` hotspots overlap `65` sectors.\n- `107` sectors have nonzero enemy-map groups.\n- `165` sectors have music override lists.\n- `430` sectors use tilesets with map-change groups.\n## Scene Composition\n`map_scene.NNNN` rows join the sector inventory to tileset and palette status. The current scene composition contract covers all `1280` scenes, `28` used tilesets, `950` direct-FTS scenes, and `330` palette-settings-only scenes.\nThe scene contract deliberately stores hashes, counts, dependency status, and feature counts instead of raw tile grids. Preview/build tools can regenerate scene payloads locally while the encyclopedia stays source-safe.\n## Editing Rule\nA map scene editor should use the scene row as the root. Editing an object, door, palette, tile animation, collision cell, music override, or enemy group should keep the sector row visible so the user understands the full scene context.\nThe current contract is an inventory and dependency layer, not a finished renderer. The next renderer can attach ignored preview outputs to these scene IDs without changing the source-safe schema.\n## Evidence Reading Order\n- [[note-notes-map-sector-bundles|Map Sector Bundle Contract]] - primary; Asset Pipeline And Manifests; Overworld Runtime; This first-pass sector contract joins the 40x32 world-sector grid to placed objects, sector metadata, tileset bundle references, door/rope/ladder/object trigger refs, enemy-map...\n- [[note-notes-map-scene-composition-contract|Map Scene Composition Contract]] - primary; Asset Pipeline And Manifests; Overworld Runtime; This contract joins sector metadata, placed scene features, tileset bundle dependencies, `.fts` component contracts, palette variants, and sector-local `map_tiles.map` tile-refe...\n- [[note-notes-map-object-bundles|Map Object Bundle Contract]] - primary; Battle Runtime; Actionscript And Event Runtime; This contract is the portable placed-object view over the current map-object work. It combines the visual role contract, movement/actionscript pointer join, map sector position,...\n- [[note-notes-map-object-layer-closure|Map Object Layer Closure]] - primary; Overworld Runtime; Asset Pipeline And Manifests; Date: 2026-04-27\n- [[note-notes-map-tileset-bundles|Map Tileset Bundle Contract]] - primary; Asset Pipeline And Manifests; Overworld Runtime; This first-pass tileset contract catalogs the EBDecomp `.fts` exports, palette-setting groups, and the sector `Tileset` IDs that depend on them.\n- [[note-notes-map-milestone-closure|Map Milestone Closure]] - primary; Asset Pipeline And Manifests; Overworld Runtime; Status: closed for the current contract/research phase.\n- [[note-notes-asset-data-contract-frontier|Asset/Data Contract Frontier]] - related; Asset Pipeline And Manifests; Overworld Runtime; Derived from checked-in `asset-manifests/*.json`, typed output recipe contracts, and contract notes. It is a phase-4 planning map: it separates byte-accounted asset data from fa...\n- [[note-notes-cf-sector-list-contracts|CF Sector List Contracts]] - related; Overworld Runtime; Validation And Tooling; Derived from `src/cf/bank_cf_helpers_asar.asm` and `src/d0/bank_d0_helpers_asar.asm`.\n- [[note-notes-bank-cf-asset-data-map|Bank CF Asset Data Map]] - related; Bank CF; Overworld Runtime; Asset Pipeline And Manifests; Derived from ebsrc bank config/source tables, `earthbound.yml`, and the local ROM.\n- [[note-notes-bank-cf-first-pass|Bank CF First Pass]] - related; Bank CF; Validation And Tooling; Battle Runtime; Bank `CF` is a generated map-data bank with a small audio tail. It is not code and not a normal binary-asset bank like `CA` through `CE`. The follow-up CF splitter now resolves...\n- [[note-notes-cf-event-music-context-contracts|CF Event Music Context Contracts]] - related; Audio And Music Data; Actionscript And Event Runtime; Derived from the byte-equivalent CF/DC source scaffolds and the C0/EF consumers.\n- [[note-notes-cf-table-splits|Bank CF Table Splits]] - related; Overworld Runtime; Actionscript And Event Runtime; Derived from ebsrc source order, eb-decompile YAML shapes, D0 cross-bank pointer tables, cross-check evidence.\n- [[note-notes-coilsnake-field-join-report|CoilSnake Field Join Report]] - related; Battle Runtime; Asset Pipeline And Manifests; Derived from `manifests/coilsnake-crosswalk.json`. Field semantics loaded from `manifests/coilsnake-field-semantics.json`. Offsets, ranges, and local anchors only; it does not c...\n- [[note-notes-coilsnake-rebuild-original-layout-report|CoilSnake Rebuild To Original Layout Report]] - related; Battle Runtime; Overworld Runtime; Generated by `tools/map_coilsnake_rebuild_to_original.py`. This report records offsets, candidate addresses, match counts, and evidence status only; it does not include ROM byte...\n- [[note-notes-data-contracts-c0-c4|Cross-bank data contract manifest]] - related; Battle Runtime; Overworld Runtime; Generated from local notes plus quarantined reference structs. This is the machine-readable struct/table front door for source and data emission work; edit `tools/build_data_con...\n- [[note-notes-position-snapshot-and-movement-tick-c0449b-c05200|Position Snapshot and Movement Tick `C0:449B-C0:5200`]] - related; Overworld Runtime; Actionscript And Event Runtime; This note covers the mid-bank `C0` cluster that sits immediately after the front-interaction probes:\n## Related Encyclopedia Entries\n- [[chapter-map-scene-contracts]]\n- [[chapter-map-object-table-contracts]]\n- [[chapter-overworld-object-asset-model]]\n- [[chapter-map-tileset-fts-contracts]]\n- [[chapter-map-palette-contracts]]\n- [[topic-overworld-runtime]]\n\n## Learning Path\nOpen [[learning-map-sector-scene-bundles|Map Sector And Scene Bundles Learning Path]] for a guided route through this chapter, its primary notes, and practical references.";
